    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0226" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00/2179</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic">December 5,
                            1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received December
                            26.</hi>]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 530</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your No. 318 of September 27, 1919,<anchor n="17" xml:id="d73-f1"/> enclosing
                    translations of two memoranda furnished the Department of State by Doctor
                    Henriquez y Carvajal concerning the situation in the Dominican Republic, and a
                    copy of a confidential memorandum of a conversation between Mr. Hallett Johnson,
                    of the Latin American Division, and Dr. Henriquez y Carvajal on the same
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I am enclosing herewith a memorandum from the Military Governor in regard to the
                    suggestions of Dr. Henriquez y Carvajal, and I fully concur in the position
                    taken therein.</p>
                <p>The Advisory Council is working in harmony with the Military Governor, and,
                    although influenced somewhat by political aspirations, apparent in the attitude
                    of the most patriotic of the Dominicans, yet, on the whole, the wisdom of the
                    appointment of the Advisory Council is being daily demonstrated.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William W.
                    Russell</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d73-a1.xml" xpointer="d73-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
